ROOM NOISE WARNING: this is the biggest practical risk in the whole talk, more than the maths. Test this exact slide in the actual room beforehand, not just at your desk. Have a pre-recorded spectrogram screenshot of the same note ready as a fallback slide if the live mic doesn’t read clearly over classroom noise.
Let the gap (or satisfying lack of one) between the predicted number from the last slide and the real measured peak here land in silence for a second before you say anything.

